From b3107a5fe272ba6d4e1a2f9e862870b01dfe634f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:08:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(heights): model-referenced heights read the setup's
 parts, never its fixtures

Top of Model and Bottom of Model resolved through solid_aabb_in, which
walks every model - vises, accessories, plates and tagged fixtures of
any setup included. A default contour in a document with a vise ran
down to the vise base and generate said ok.

Both references (and their "no model loaded" diagnostic) now read
setup_align::part_aabb_in: every non-fixture model in the asking
setup's frame. solid_aabb_in, is_model and the collision laws are
unchanged, so verify still strikes a pass into the vise.

Pinned by tests/heights_fixtures.rs (five tests, mutation-checked).

Fixes #1529

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
